## Topics

research method, interview technique, review mining, awareness levels, market
sophistication, objection discovery, jobs and trigger moments, off label use,
segmentation, avatar record structure.

## Look for

The method, step by step. How many interviews or reviews are enough. Which questions
produce garbage. How to tell a real job from a stated preference. How to find segments
nobody targets. The exact structure of a usable avatar record.

## Skip

Persona templates with demographic fields and no job. Anything producing a fictional
character with a stock photo. B2B ideal-customer-profile content unless it carries a
job statement.

**Watch for re-cuts.** The same creator publishing the same avatar method 4 times with
4 different revenue numbers in the title is 1 source, not 4.

## Scope mix

The method is universal, so there is a real baseline: every avatar must carry quoted
evidence, a trigger moment and a job statement. Reject any avatar lacking all 3. The
number of avatars is not universal.

## Why this folder matters most

Every page, ad, email and offer downstream inherits whatever this produces. Highest
value per source in the library.

